 ## Mechanism
 
-`build-kit` creates an external, non-repository run root containing an unpacked Manifest V3 Chromium-family extension, the exact admitted probe, two body-free controller templates, a named-human confirmation template, the frozen profile, all measured verification programs, a source-binding receipt, a deterministic kit manifest, and a private runbook. The extension contract requires the admitted probe to execute at `document_start` in the page `MAIN` world. Continuous integration may build and verify this kit, but it does not launch a browser, contact an endpoint, download a model, form a peer connection, or perform inference.
+`build-kit` creates an external, non-repository run root containing an unpacked Manifest V3 Chromium-family extension, the exact admitted probe, two body-free controller templates, a named-human confirmation template, the frozen profile, all measured verification programs, a source-binding receipt, a deterministic kit manifest, and a private runbook. The extension contract requires the admitted probe to execute at `document_start` in the page `MAIN` world. The builder also materializes the same exact probe at `source/browser_distributed_inference_probe.js`, which is the dependency coordinate used by the standalone packet runtime documented in the runbook. Kit verification binds both copies to the admitted SHA-256 value, requires byte identity between them, verifies the complete `kitSourceBindings` denominator under `source/`, and refuses a missing, substituted, divergent, or extra runtime member. Continuous integration may build and verify this kit, but it does not launch a browser, contact an endpoint, download a model, form a peer connection, or perform inference.
 
 Each completed private packet contains exactly two independently captured seat records. Every seat retains a raw probe export and a controller object privately. The compiler materializes each capture through the exact 